        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(tts): guard persona provider isConfigured against malformed config throws",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`resolvePrimaryTtsProviderCandidate` calls `provider.isConfigured()` without try/catch protection. When a provider throws from its `isConfigured` implementation (e.g. Gradium on a malformed `baseUrl`), the exception bypasses the `not_configured` skip result and propagates to the persona resolution caller, hiding every other usable provider behind one broken one.\n\nThis is the sibling of #108569 which fixed the same throw-in-isConfigured pattern in `resolveTtsProviderCandidates`.\n\n## Fix\n\nWrap the `isConfigured` probe in try/catch. A thrown exception now defaults `providerConfigured` to `undefined` (falsy), producing the same `{ kind: \"skip\", reasonCode: \"not_configured\" }` result as a provider that reports unconfigured.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Before fix\n\nA provider whose `isConfigured` throws (e.g. Gradium with invalid baseUrl):\n```\nresolvePrimaryTtsProviderCandidate() → throw \"Gradium baseUrl must target api.gradium.ai\"\n```\nThe persona resolution crashes. No other provider is tried.\n\n### After fix\n\n```\nresolvePrimaryTtsProviderCandidate() → { kind: \"skip\", reasonCode: \"not_configured\" }\n```\nPersona resolution continues to the next candidate.\n\n### Vitest output (47/47 tests pass)\n\n```\n$ npx vitest run packages/speech-core/src/tts.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  47 passed (47)\n```\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Existing 47 tests still pass (no regression)\n- [x] `resolveTtsProviderCandidates` was already guarded by #108569\n- [x] `resolvePrimaryTtsProviderCandidate` is now also guarded — same pattern, same file",
        "branch": "fix/tts-persona-isconfigured-guard",
